<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro de San Superano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1402</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro de San Superano was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/navarrese-company">Navarrese Company</a>, a band of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> that seized much of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> from the late 1370s. He ruled as vicar and from 1396 as prince of Achaea until his death in 1402, after which his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-ii-zaccaria">Maria II Zaccaria</a> succeeded.</p></div>
